### How to run

On your local machine, with an existing SSH key:
```sh
export SPEC_SSH_KEY="$HOME/.ssh/opencode-dev-aue_ed25519"
ssh -i "$SPEC_SSH_KEY" -o ExitOnForwardFailure=yes \
  -L 127.0.0.1:4780:127.0.0.1:4780 opencode@build-host
```
Verify the host-key fingerprint before accepting a new host key.

Inside the remote shell:
```sh
cd ~/spec
git status --short
git switch dev && git pull --ff-only origin dev

SPEC_COMMAND="$HOME/.local/bin/spec" \
SPEC_WORKSPACE="$HOME/specs" \
SPEC_PORT=4780 ./run.sh
```

Open the printed localhost URL, including its token, in your local browser. **Save & run** executes `spec build` remotely with automatic tool approval.

